item.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;hs-featured-image-wrapper&quot;&gt; 
 &lt;a class=&quot;hs-featured-image-link&quot; href=&quot;https://blog.pcisecuritystandards.org/the-ai-exchange-innovators-in-payment-security-featuring-shopify&quot; title=&quot;&quot;&gt; &lt;img alt=&quot;The AI Exchange: Innovators in Payment Security Featuring Shopify&quot; class=&quot;hs-featured-image&quot; src=&quot;https://blog.pcisecuritystandards.org/hubfs/2026-blog/shopify-blog.jpg&quot; style=&quot;width: auto !important; float: left; margin: 0 15px 15px 0;&quot; /&gt; &lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;/div&gt; 
&lt;br /&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the PCI Security Standards Council’s blog series, The AI Exchange: Innovators in Payment Security. This special, ongoing feature of our PCI Perspectives blog offers a resource for payment security industry stakeholders to exchange information about how they are adopting and implementing artificial intelligence (AI) into their organizations. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In both a 2021 &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.belfercenter.org/publication/coming-ai-hackers&quot;&gt;essay&lt;/a&gt; and my 2022 book, &lt;i&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.schneier.com/books/a-hackers-mind/&quot;&gt;A Hacker&amp;#8217;s Mind&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/i&gt;, I talk about AIs finding vulnerabilities and exploits&amp;#8212;hacking&amp;#8212;the legal system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.felixringe.com/legal-exploits/&quot;&gt;Here&amp;#8217;s&lt;/a&gt; some demonstrations of this from Germany:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Legal systems encode the foundations of social order in natural language. Similar to computer systems, the written law can contain vulnerabilities that invite exploitation.1 Courts absorb most exploits through interpretation, and such vulnerabilities rarely surface in the first place. With highly capable AI systems enabling the discovery of vulnerabilities at unprecedented scale, we believe the latter could change...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/NickADobos/status/2113430301183823901&quot;&gt;comment&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;3% of &amp;#8216;critical&amp;#8217; software security bugs, in all of recorded history, have been found in the last month. This is on pace to find another ~100,000 bugs this year alone, adding ~26% more vulnerabilities to the all time total Do you realize how fucking insane that is?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yes. It is a new world out there.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Neat &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/watch-an-elusive-and-ethereal-bigfin-squid-float-above-the-seafloor-off-central-california-180989491/&quot;&gt;video&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;The sighting, announced September 2, marks the first time anyone has spotted a live bigfin squid, which belongs to the &lt;i&gt;Magnapinna&lt;/i&gt; genus, in the northeastern Pacific Ocean.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As usual, you can also use this squid post to talk about the security stories in the news that I haven&amp;#8217;t covered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.schneier.com/blog/archives/2024/06/new-blog-moderation-policy.html&quot;&gt;Blog moderation policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thedrive.com/news/cheap-aftermarket-head-units-are-loaded-with-spyware-by-the-way&quot;&gt;story&lt;/a&gt; is interesting:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;One Civic owner purchased a cheap aftermarket head unit off Amazon, and decided to have Claude work its magic on it, like it would a smart TV. What was reportedly discovered isn’t surprising, but is worth knowing about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Among the pre-installed bloatware&amp;#8212;­or spyware, if you’re being less charitable­&amp;#8212;was a voice assistant equipped with WebView, an Android system component that lets apps display content off the web. This apparently always used about a third of processing power, even while idle, which isn’t great. There were also Baidu location services, a call recorder (!), a DAB radio client that is pretty much useless in the U.S., and Adobe Acrobat, presumably so your passenger can entertain themselves with PDFs on the go...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
